1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,600
[Episode 15]

3
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,400
The police have obtained new leads

4
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:16,230
on Han Shuang's disappearance
seven years ago.

5
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:18,430
I know.

6
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:20,040
What I want to know is

7
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,790
whether your approach is working.

8
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,280
He's starting to waver.

9
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,480
Give me a little more time.

10
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,840
He'll give up.

11
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:28,040
I can't wait.

12
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:30,000
The police have come to us already.

13
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,350
You're dealing with the police now.

14
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:35,430
Only my way leaves them no evidence.

15
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,590
Even if they get evidence on you,

16
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:46,200
you'll have to deal with it yourself.

17
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:49,280
After all,
I pay your brother's medical bills.

18
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,150
As long as the police don't suspect me,

19
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,400
I'll keep your brother alive.

20
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:58,150
Think carefully about what you must do.

21
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:02,430
Okay.
I understand.

22
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:48,800
You used the computer?

23
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:50,750
Oh.

24
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,470
I was just reading the news.

25
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:34,080
I'm always pushing you to sleep early
and get up early.

26
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,280
What's gotten into you today?

27
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:40,870
I suddenly realized you were right.

28
00:03:43,150 --> 00:03:46,750
I guess a man really can grow up
overnight.

29
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:48,680
But you didn't have to do all this.

30
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,680
I rarely have friends over.

31
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:52,680
I can do a little tidying myself.

32
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,750
You need to get more rest.

33
00:03:57,190 --> 00:03:58,680
I should help lighten your load.

34
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:02,150
After all, you don't earn money
just for yourself.

35
00:04:02,630 --> 00:04:04,750
You also have me, this burden.

36
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:10,240
You brat.
Don't say that.

37
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:14,000
Don't worry.
I can support you.

38
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:21,480
My treatment cost over a million yuan.

39
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:23,000
Where did all that money come from?

40
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,870
It hasn't cost that much.

41
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,070
Once a donor match is found,

42
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:31,480
you won't need dialysis anymore.

43
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,870
Then you can find something to do

44
00:04:34,430 --> 00:04:35,560
and give me less to worry about.

45
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:21,870
I'm looking for someone.

46
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,160
Hi.

47
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:25,630
Could I ask you about someone?

48
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,430
I have a question.

49
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:29,680
Is there a nurse named Xu Manman here?

50
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,270
One moment.
I'll ask around for you.

51
00:05:31,390 --> 00:05:32,040
Hey.

52
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,750
Excuse me, sir.

53
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:33,830
Could I ask you about someone?

54
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:34,430
Sure.
Go ahead.

55
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:35,600
Xiaojing.

56
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:38,270
She hasn't come to work in a while.

57
00:05:38,430 --> 00:05:40,830
This student named Shu Qi...

58
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,430
Does she work at this bar?

59
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,950
Her summer break wasn't even over

60
00:05:43,950 --> 00:05:45,000
when she stopped working here.

61
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,870
Does Zheng Jiajia live in this building?

62
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:48,390
I haven't seen her in quite a while.

63
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,830
You mean Xu Manman?

64
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:51,190
She hasn't come to work in ages.

65
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:53,070
We don't know why either.

66
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,480
Why did dialysis take so long today?

67
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:14,070
Were you feeling unwell?

68
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:18,680
Oh,
I chatted with a classmate for a while.

69
00:06:19,430 --> 00:06:20,800
You're even socializing now?

70
00:06:21,870 --> 00:06:23,560
All right.
I'll cook for you.

71
00:06:23,830 --> 00:06:24,870
I'm not hungry.

72
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:27,630
Did you eat out?

73
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,480
Uh...

74
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:31,630
Sis.

75
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:33,830
I need to tell you something.

76
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:38,870
I need to take this call.

77
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:39,680
We'll talk when I get back.

78
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,480
What is it?

79
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:57,160
Make up any excuse.

80
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:00,270
Get that cop to the corner bar
in Taishan.

81
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:02,070
Does it have to be tonight?

82
00:07:02,070 --> 00:07:04,480
Yes.
We can't risk further delays.

83
00:07:05,390 --> 00:07:07,800
I'll tell you the rest
when you get there.

84
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,950
What are you going to do to him?

85
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,480
Don't ask.

86
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,160
Think about your brother.

87
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,480
What were you going to ask me?

88
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,430
Sis, tell me.

89
00:07:57,830 --> 00:07:59,070
What are these files for?

90
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:02,360
And what does Luoda Biotech do?

91
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:07,830
These are just patient records.

92
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,680
Patient records?

93
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,560
Then why are they all girls?

94
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:16,750
Huh?

95
00:08:18,190 --> 00:08:20,000
Why did they never return to school

96
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:21,750
after meeting you,

97
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,830
never go home,

98
00:08:24,070 --> 00:08:25,800
or ever appear again?

99
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,670
I couldn't just watch you die.

100
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:35,080
I had no choice.

101
00:08:36,670 --> 00:08:37,960
What did you do to them?

102
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:41,480
I didn't do anything.

103
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,630
I only passed their information
to someone else.

104
00:08:44,630 --> 00:08:46,600
Who?

105
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:49,790
I can't tell you.

106
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:56,550
Sis.

107
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:03,750
They were as desperate as I am.

108
00:09:05,870 --> 00:09:07,480
You were their only lifeline.

109
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:10,270
They trusted you.

110
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:13,000
But look how you treated them!

111
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:19,000
I don't care about anyone else.

112
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,440
I only want you to be okay.

113
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:23,200
Nothing else matters to me.

114
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:28,670
Xiaowei.

115
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:53,360
Another one.

116
00:09:57,870 --> 00:09:59,030
You're still drinking?

117
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:00,480
You've had too much.

118
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:02,670
You got here fast.

119
00:10:05,790 --> 00:10:07,670
Didn't you promise to drink with me?

120
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:10,960
You're drunk.
I'll take you home.

121
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:16,030
Why aren't you asking why I called you?

122
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,750
Whatever you say now,

123
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:20,670
I won't believe it.

124
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,670
We'll talk when you're sober.

125
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,840
Let's go.

126
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:28,790
Sure.

127
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:32,360
But promise you'll come upstairs
for a while.

128
00:10:37,550 --> 00:10:39,670
Okay.
Let's go.

129
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,200
Easy.
Easy.

130
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,000
Hmph.

131
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,270
What?

132
00:10:58,790 --> 00:10:59,360
Water.

133
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:01,270
I want some water.

134
00:11:01,390 --> 00:11:02,080
Water?

135
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,840
Mm.

136
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:04,600
Okay.
Wait here.

137
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,120
I'll buy you some.

138
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:05,630
Mm.

139
00:12:03,410 --> 00:12:05,470
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

140
00:12:05,470 --> 00:12:07,420
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

141
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:09,330
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

142
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:11,130
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

143
00:12:11,130 --> 00:12:13,470
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

144
00:12:13,470 --> 00:12:15,890
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

145
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:20,950
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

146
00:12:20,950 --> 00:12:22,840
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

147
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,790
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

148
00:12:24,790 --> 00:12:26,910
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

149
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:28,920
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

150
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:31,080
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

151
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:38,160
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

152
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:41,530
♪Why is that child crying?♪

153
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,230
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

154
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:45,850
♪Means I've grown up♪

155
00:12:45,850 --> 00:12:48,990
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

156
00:12:48,990 --> 00:12:52,480
♪The wound still aches♪

157
00:12:52,890 --> 00:12:57,240
♪Like a biting winter♪

158
00:12:57,240 --> 00:13:00,500
♪But a spark still glows♪

